    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/08/asics-sonicblast-review-2025.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The 46/38 mm high-stack setup gives strong impact protection, but the ride is relatively firm; heel landings can feel bumpy/clunky at easy paces while the forefoot feels smoother.",
        "Responsiveness: Forefoot response is a standout, with lively energy return, sharp rocker-assisted roll, and a big bounce/snappy feel at uptempo and faster efforts.",
        "Stability: The 3/4-length Pebax plate and generally stiff platform provide high torsional rigidity and solid lockdown, though the rigid midfoot/heel geometry can make slower transitions awkward.",
        "Durability: Outsole uses grippy high-abrasion rubber and the review’s durability expectation is above average, indicating good wear resistance and material longevity."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/08/asics-sonicblast-review-4-comparisons.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: 46/38 mm stack with FF Turbo Squared is described as highly cushioned, soft, and protective, with especially poppy forefoot feel; heel landings can feel firmer or overly rigid at slower paces.",
        "Responsiveness: FF Turbo Squared plus the nylon/fiberglass Astroplate gives energetic bounce and moderate-to-strong propulsion/snappiness, feeling lively but generally controlled rather than harsh.",
        "Stability: Testers found it stable for a max-stack shoe due to controlled geometry, near-rigid rocker, stabilizing lower foam, and supportive upper/lockdown (some used the extra eyelet for better ankle hold).",
        "Durability: The provided text gives no meaningful outsole wear or long-term material longevity results, so durability is not established in this excerpt."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/asics-sonicblast-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The 46 mm heel / 38 mm forefoot stack with FF Turbo Squared over FF Blast Max gives a soft-yet-springy feel, strong impact protection, and a smooth, well-cushioned heel-to-forefoot ride without feeling mushy.",
        "Responsiveness: The Pebax Astroplate and lively foam setup provide clear energy return, bounce, and noticeable snap/pop, helping the shoe handle both easy paces and uptempo efforts.",
        "Stability: For a high-stack trainer it feels planted and controlled, with plate-induced rigidity, a supportive heel counter/lockdown, and solid lateral steadiness (though it is not a true stability shoe).",
        "Durability: AsicsGrip outsole showed only light scuffing after 30+ miles, suggesting good early durability, with the main long-term question being exposed FF Blast Max foam wear."
      ]
    }
